mcp-client-state-notConnected = Not connected yet.
mcp-client-state-connected = Already connected.
mcp-client-state-outdated = Connected, but the entry is outdated (for example a different program path).
mcp-client-state-blocked = The file cannot be changed.
mcp-client-extra-keys = The existing entry contains your own additions ({ $keys }). “Update” replaces the whole entry; afterwards the additions are only in the backup.
mcp-client-file = Configuration file: { $path }
mcp-allow-crawl = Agent may start crawls
mcp-allow-crawl-help = Reading is always allowed. The permission applies to all connected programs and can be changed on the Tools tab.
mcp-connect = Connect
mcp-update = Update
mcp-disconnect = Disconnect
mcp-copy-entry = Copy entry
mcp-entry-copied = Entry copied to the clipboard, for pasting into the program’s configuration by hand.
mcp-show-changes = Show changes
mcp-changes-help = Changed lines only; secrets of other entries are masked. All other lines of the file stay unchanged.
mcp-client-done-connected = Connected. Start a new session in { $program } so that OpenSpider appears there.
mcp-client-done-unchanged = Already connected; the file is unchanged. Start a new session in { $program } if OpenSpider is still missing there.
mcp-client-done-disconnected = Disconnected. Start a new session in { $program }.
mcp-client-done-connected-reload = Connected. Reload the MCP servers in { $program } or restart { $program } so that OpenSpider appears there.
mcp-client-done-unchanged-reload = Already connected; the file is unchanged. Reload the MCP servers in { $program } if OpenSpider is still missing there.
mcp-client-done-disconnected-reload = Disconnected. Reload the MCP servers in { $program }.
mcp-client-problem-syntax = The file is not valid JSON or TOML (line { $line }; e.g. comments). OpenSpider does not change it. Check the file in the program, or copy the entry and paste it by hand.
mcp-client-problem-unsupported = The file is valid, but structured in a way that OpenSpider cannot change the entry without rewriting other lines. Copy the entry and paste it by hand.
mcp-client-problem-symlink = The configuration file is a symbolic link. OpenSpider does not write through links. Copy the entry and paste it by hand.
mcp-client-problem-readOnly = The configuration file is read-only. OpenSpider does not change it. Remove the write protection, or copy the entry and paste it by hand.
mcp-client-changed = Another program changed the file while connecting. Nothing was written; try again.
mcp-client-write-failed = The configuration file could not be replaced, for example because another program has it open. It is unchanged, and the backup was removed again. Try again, or copy the entry and paste it by hand.
mcp-client-write-failed-backup = The configuration file could not be replaced and is unchanged. The backup { $path } could not be removed; it holds the previous content, including other programs’ credentials. Please delete it by hand.
mcp-diff = Configuration diff
mcp-no-changes = No changes needed.
mcp-backup = Backup: { $path }
